  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Basically, techically fallbacks CAN have physbones on PC, and contacts if under the limits for PC and Quest. Fallbacks are able to have custom gestures, FX layers, animations, etc. Lets say I use a contact for my fallback to detect when a player approaches from behind. I attempted to display a custom blendshape sign stating that the avatar was in-fact a fallback when the torso or head was in the contact. The avatar worked fine when testing and actually having the avatar set as the in-use avatar. However when it's in a fallback situation when in an unoptimized avatar the contacts will no longer work.",
